quran[14]{c,v,t}:
  109,1,Say: ‘O disbelievers!
  109,2,"I do not worship what you worship,"
  109,3,nor do you worship what I worship.
  109,4,"And I will never worship what you worship,"
  109,5,nor will you worship what I worship.
  109,6,"You have your religion, and I have my religion.’"
  110,1,"When Allah’s help comes and the victory,"
  110,2,"and you see the people entering Allah’s Religion in crowds,"
  110,3,"then glorify the praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness. Indeed, He is Most-Clement."
  111,1,"May the hands of Abu Lahab perish, and he (himself) perish!"
  111,2,Neither his wealth nor what he earns will avail him.
  111,3,"He shall soon enter the Fire with blazing flame,"
  111,4,"and his wife (too), the firewood carrier,"
  111,5,with a rope of palm fibre around her neck (that she used to bind thorny twigs to).
